+{
+  "task_id": "T25",
+  "repository": "wattclaw",
+  "mode": "contract",
+  "evidence": [
+    {
+      "path": "server/core/session-sync.js",
+      "symbol": "syncUserSessionsFromGateway",
+      "start_line": 118,
+      "end_line": 178,
+      "observation": "Single sync pass for one user. It resolves the owned/admin agent ids, lists gateway sessions per agent through sessions.list (bounded by perAgentLimit, agents fetched with mapWithConcurrency), normalizes every raw delivery, drops keys whose agent is outside the ownership set or that are in recentlyDeletedSessionKeys, and then delegates each surviving delivery to upsertSyncedUserSession. The pass increments changed/inserted/updated ONLY when the upsert reports result.changed (lines 162-168), so replaying an already-applied session update adds nothing to the change counters even though scanned still counts each delivery. The returned report { changed, inserted, updated, scanned, agents } is therefore the idempotency surface: a duplicated event can only ever move 'scanned'."
+    },
+    {
+      "path": "server/core/session-sync.js",
+      "symbol": "scheduleUserSessionSync",
+      "start_line": 179,
+      "end_line": 216,
+      "observation": "Duplicate-event guard around the sync pass. A replayed event that arrives inside cooldownMs returns { changed: 0, skipped: true, reason: 'cooldown' } without touching the gateway (lines 188-193), and a duplicate event that arrives while the same user's sync is still running receives the SAME in-flight promise from inFlightByUserId (lines 195-197, 214) instead of starting a second scan. The promise is registered synchronously (line 214) and removed in .finally (lines 210-212), and lastSyncAtByUserId is stamped only after success (lines 202-205), so a replayed event cannot produce a duplicate state change or a duplicate gateway round-trip."
+    },
+    {
+      "path": "server/core/session-sync.js",
+      "symbol": "normalizeGatewaySessionForSync",
+      "start_line": 59,
+      "end_line": 77,
+      "observation": "Deterministic mapping from a raw gateway session envelope (key/sessionKey/session_key/id, agentId/agent_id/agent, displayTitle/label/title/name, lastMessageAt/last_message_at/updatedAt/...) to exactly { sessionKey, agentId, channel, peer, label, lastActivity }. Identical inputs always normalize to identical fields, which is what makes the replay comparison in upsertSyncedUserSession stable instead of flapping between 'inserted' and 'updated' for the same event."
+    },
+    {
+      "path": "server/core/session-sync.js",
+      "symbol": "DEFAULT_SESSION_SYNC_OPTIONS",
+      "start_line": 7,
+      "end_line": 12,
+      "observation": "Frozen defaults for the sync contract: perAgentLimit 50, cooldownMs 60_000, overallTimeoutMs 8_000, gatewayConcurrency 2. The 60s cooldown is the concrete window in which a replayed session update is dropped by scheduleUserSessionSync, and gatewayConcurrency bounds how many agents (never how many times one session is applied) are listed concurrently."
+    },
+    {
+      "path": "server/user-manager.js",
+      "symbol": "upsertSyncedUserSession",
+      "start_line": 614,
+      "end_line": 689,
